  "subject": {
    "id": "pack-grounding-compiler-alignment",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "Align project grounding with compiler reference semantics.",
  "why": "The grounding rite previously missed Malleus roots written as compiler-accepted CURIEs, while the binder misread unrelated grounding annotations as adoption markers. The correction gives the rite one explicit root namespace, resolves only source-declared prefixes against it, and enters adoption logic only when the adopts field exists. Executable documentation now uses the accepted annotation shape and the live immutable-receipt guard."
}
